  "note": "Triennial election of Belfast Corporation, polled Wednesday 21 May 1958: 90 candidates for 53 seats (45 councillors and the aldermen of eight wards); contests in 13 of the 15 wards (Belfast News-Letter, 8 and 9 May 1958). Victoria Ward's councillors were elected on 19 June 1958 (separate folder) after the death of a candidate. Unionist gain from Labour (Mrs Barter's seat confirmed after a recount). The Irish News prints J. D. Barbour and 1,418 for Mrs Barter. Spoiled papers 213 in the councillors' poll (174 in the aldermanic poll)."
